The validation of tasks enforcing this behavior was introduced in https://github.com/bacalhau-project/bacalhau/pull/2802 and has thus been present since roughly [v1.1.0](https://github.com/bacalhau-project/bacalhau/releases/tag/v1.1.0).

@wdbaruni is the acceptance criteria here to 1) modify the Tasks `ValidateSubmission` method such that it is only called after the job has been transformed server side 2) modify the transformer to check if results path is defined before applying a default publisher? I believe this change may need to be landed with https://github.com/bacalhau-project/bacalhau/issues/4392 since automatically including a results path in docker jobs will cause validation of the task to fail - an is likely the reason the default was removed.
We discussed this over our 1:1. Just moving the validation from ValidateSubmission to Validate will be enough

