hints_text:
Thanks for the issue @daviddavis, and for the kind words! 

I agree, this would be a great feature to add -- I'd be happy to have it return with the following codes:

1. `0`: no warnings/errors at all;
2. `11`: all warnings are "low" or below;
3. `12`: all warnings are "medium" or below;
4. `13`: there's at least one "high"

(The reason I suggest starting at `11` is because I don't want to shadow any existing - incidental - low error code behavior: I think currently we exit with `1` on any internal tool failures.)

If you'd be interested in sending a PR for this, I'd be happy to review it! Otherwise, I can tackle this myself in the next day or so.
(Also thinking out loud: I'm not 100% sure if exit codes should be used with `--format=sarif` -- some tools might treat an exit code in that case as an error within the tool itself. But we can start out by making exit codes universal and seeing what happens 🙂)
That all sounds good to me. 👍

