problem_statement:
Miss pk identify in some cases in GOpt
**Describe the bug**

Currently, in the GOpt-based compilation, the following query (on LDBC graph with "Person"'s "id" as pk) missed pk optimization in the plan:
```
g.V().has("PERSON", "id", 19791209300143)
```
The plan looks like:
```
  "plan": [{
    "opr": {
      "scan": {
        "params": {
          "tables": [{
            "id": 1
          }],
          "predicate": {
            "operators": [{
              "var": {
                "property": {
                  "key": {
                    "name": "id"
                  }
                },
                "nodeType": {
                  "dataType": "INT64"
                }
              },
              "nodeType": {
                "dataType": "INT64"
              }
            }, {
              "logical": "EQ",
              "nodeType": {
                "dataType": "BOOLEAN"
              }
            }, {
              "const": {
                "i64": "19791209300143"
              },
              "nodeType": {
                "dataType": "INT64"
              }
            }]
          },
          "sampleRatio": 1.0
        }
      }
    },
...
}
```

While the following query can correctly identify pk:
```
g.V().hasLabel("PERSON").has("id", 19791209300143)
```
The plan looks like:
```
  "plan": [{
    "opr": {
      "scan": {
        "params": {
          "tables": [{
            "id": 1
          }],
          "sampleRatio": 1.0
        },
        "idxPredicate": {
          "orPredicates": [{
            "predicates": [{
              "key": {
                "key": {
                  "name": "id"
                }
              },
              "const": {
                "i64": "19791209300143"
              }
            }]
          }]
        }
      }
    },
...
}
```

